# Cloudflare Pages headers.
#
# Cloudflare Pages COMBINES (appends) the headers from every matching rule rather
# than overriding by specificity — so setting the same header name on both /* and
# /admin/* produces DUPLICATE headers. To keep exactly one of each, the security
# headers are set ONCE globally on /*, and the /admin rules add ONLY Cache-Control.
#
# DELIBERATELY NO content CSP (default-src / script-src / style-src / connect-src):
# it would break inline JSON-LD, inline styles, Google Fonts, and the cross-origin
# POSTs to scdesign-wirral.vercel.app + q-cbuild1.vercel.app. A future content CSP
# MUST allow-list fonts.googleapis.com + fonts.gstatic.com (style/font),
# 'unsafe-inline' (JSON-LD + inline styles), and connect-src those two vercel.app
# origins — or the live site breaks. HSTS is SHORT (no includeSubDomains, no
# preload) until every scdesignwirral.co.uk subdomain is confirmed HTTPS-only.
/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Content-Security-Policy: frame-ancestors 'none'
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=(), payment=()
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=300

# Admin portal: never cache the app shell, scripts or styles (always run the
# latest code / show live data). Frame protection comes from /* above — do NOT
# repeat X-Frame-Options / CSP here or Cloudflare emits duplicate headers.
/admin
  Cache-Control: no-store, max-age=0
/admin/*
  Cache-Control: no-store, max-age=0

# /samantha — PRIVATE DESIGN SANDBOX (Wallasey Trusted Home Cleans draft).
# Must NEVER be indexed, cached by a search engine, summarised by an AI crawler,
# or have its images picked up. X-Robots-Tag is the belt; the page's own <meta
# name="robots"> and the Disallow in src/app/robots.ts are the braces. Deleting
# any one of the three weakens it — change all three together or none.
# no-store also means a design change is visible on refresh, with no CDN lag.
# Security headers come from /* above — do NOT repeat them here (Cloudflare
# Pages APPENDS matching rules, so a repeat emits duplicate headers).
/samantha
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex, nofollow, noarchive, nosnippet, noimageindex
  Cache-Control: no-store, max-age=0
/samantha/*
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex, nofollow, noarchive, nosnippet, noimageindex
  Cache-Control: no-store, max-age=0

# >>> MTCW preview >>>
# /MTCW - design preview of a separate concept site, parked on this host for
# review (same arrangement as /WVROOFING). Unlisted and never indexed: this
# X-Robots-Tag plus every page's own <meta name="robots">; no robots.txt entry,
# sitemap, llms.txt line or link on this site points to it. Security headers
# come from /* above and are NOT repeated (Cloudflare Pages appends matching
# rules). Content-Security-Policy is the one name shared with /*: browsers
# enforce every CSP they receive, so /*'s frame-ancestors policy and this
# stricter preview policy (same-origin only, no inline script) both apply.
# Written by the MTCW project's scripts/deploy-preview.mjs, which replaces
# everything between these markers on each run: change it there, not here.
/MTCW
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex, nofollow, noarchive, nosnippet, noimageindex
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self'; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; img-src 'self' data:; font-src 'self'; connect-src 'self'; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self'; frame-ancestors 'none'
/MTCW/*
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex, nofollow, noarchive, nosnippet, noimageindex
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self'; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; img-src 'self' data:; font-src 'self'; connect-src 'self'; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self'; frame-ancestors 'none'
